      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nCoastal detached three-bedroom residence set on 0.56 acres approx., enjoying breathtaking panoramic views across Glandore Harbour and the iconic 'Adam & Eve' islands. The property is located in one of West Cork's most prestigious locations. \n\nConstructed in 2007 / 2008, the property has a B BER rating and is thoughtfully designed to maximise natural light, generous living space and its remarkable coastal setting. Extending to approximately 186 sq.m. (2,005 sq.ft.), the accommodation offers an ideal balance of elegant reception rooms and practical family living, with the principal rooms carefully positioned to capture the spectacular sea views.\n\nA welcoming entrance porch provides a cloakroom and houses the alarm system and the controls for the external EV charging point. Beyond, the impressive entrance hall creates a wonderful sense of space, featuring a magnificent handcrafted oak staircase, solid oak flooring and understairs storage. The heart of the home is undoubtedly the stunning open-plan kitchen / dining room. This exceptional double-height space is flooded with light and enjoys beautiful views towards the outer harbour. Finished with quality fitted units, generous work surfaces and a central island, it provides the perfect setting for family life and entertaining. A pantry and separate utility room are located off the kitchen, with the utility also providing access to the attic. The beautifully proportioned sitting room is bright and inviting, featuring a raised fireplace with a wood-burning stove and large glazed doors opening onto the patio and gardens. The ground floor also accommodates a bedroom with ensuite which and is currently in use as a study.\n\nOn the first floor there are two exceptionally generous bedrooms. The impressive principal suite features a luxurious ensuite bathroom, while the guest bedroom also benefits from its own ensuite. All three bedrooms are fitted with bespoke built-in wardrobes.\n\nOutside, the property is equally impressive. The beautifully landscaped gardens feature expansive lawns, mature planting and numerous seating areas from which to enjoy the magnificent coastal surroundings. Two gated entrances (one electric) provide convenient access from either side of the property, while the sweeping driveway offers extensive parking and turning space.\n\nA detached garage with electric roller door provides excellent storage and workshop facilities, while the property also benefits from a glasshouse, raised vegetable beds and a garden shed—ideal for those wishing to embrace a sustainable lifestyle. Solar panels further enhance the home's excellent energy efficiency.\n\nSituated in one of West Cork's most coveted coastal settings, the property offers the perfect combination of tranquillity and convenience. The picturesque harbour village of Glandore, renowned for its sailing, waterfront restaurants and vibrant community, is just moments away, while Rosscarbery and the larger market town of Skibbereen are within easy reach, providing an excellent range of schools, shops and everyday amenities. Whether as a permanent family home or an exceptional coastal retreat, this is a rare opportunity to acquire a beautifully appointed residence in one of Ireland's most scenic and desirable locations.\n\nDisclaimer: \nWhilst every care has been taken in the preparation of these particulars, all information is provided in good faith and is believed to be correct, but is not guaranteed. Interested parties should satisfy themselves as to the accuracy and completeness of all details by independent inspection or enquiry. No representation or warranty is made regarding the condition, measurements, boundaries, planning status, services or other information relating to the property. All measurements, maps, photographs and distances are approximate and for guidance purposes only. Photographs, video and drone imagery are provided for illustrative purposes and may include features, furnishings or items not included in the sale."
